### Description

Initiate an approval for launching a job plan. This API only creates an approval task and runs a full pre-check on the parameters. **The job plan is not launched.** Once the approval is granted, Job launches it automatically as the creator of the task.

Before calling: the target job plan must exist and the caller must have the permission to view and launch it in the resource scope. If the pre-check fails, an error is returned and no approval task is created.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| approval_channel | string | No | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel). The default channel configured on the server is used when omitted. Only the channel enum can be specified; the channel address and secret always come from the server configuration |
| job_plan_id | long | Yes | ID of the job plan to launch |
| global_var_list | array | No | Global variable values. All default values defined in the job plan are used when omitted |
| callback_url | string | No | Callback URL invoked after the job finishes, at most 1024 characters. Job calls it once the released job completes |
| start_task | boolean | No | Whether to start the job immediately after the approval is granted. Options: `true` (start immediately, the default), `false` (only create the job instance without starting it) |

##### global_var_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| id | long | No | Global variable ID. Provide either `id` or `name`; this one wins if both are given |
| name | string | No | Global variable name. Provide either `id` or `name` |
| value | string | No | Global variable value. Use `execute_target` for an execution-target variable and this field for the other types (string, namespace, ciphertext, associative array, indexed array). A ciphertext variable is shown as a placeholder in the approval ticket |
| execute_target | object | No | Value of an execution-target global variable |

##### execute_target

{% include '_generic_v4_execute_target.md.j2' %}

**Note:** When the value contains dynamic groups or topology nodes, the actual number of execution objects is resolved again at release time and may differ from the moment of initiation; the approval ticket highlights this explicitly.

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "approval_channel": "IMATE",
    "job_plan_id": 50001,
    "global_var_list": [
        {
            "id": 300001,
            "value": "/data/release"
        },
        {
            "name": "DB_PASSWORD",
            "value": "p@ssw0rd"
        },
        {
            "name": "HOST_TARGET",
            "execute_target": {
                "host_list": [
                    {
                        "bk_host_id": 10001
                    },
                    {
                        "bk_cloud_id": 0,
                        "ip": "127.0.0.2"
                    }
                ],
                "dynamic_group_list": [
                    {
                        "id": "asdo8gojhasdfskft7pr5"
                    }
                ],
                "topo_node_list": [
                    {
                        "id": 1000,
                        "node_type": "module"
                    }
                ]
            }
        }
    ],
    "callback_url": "https://example.com/job/callback",
    "start_task": true
}
```

